 * 2. Log in as that admin to obtain JWT (auth handled auto by SDK)
 * 3. Create a moderation event, required for the new appeal
 * 4. Create an appeal record, linked to the moderation event and admin as appellant
 * 5. Execute the soft delete (erase) operation on the appeal
 * 6. [Not available: There is no standard query/get API for appeals, so we are unable to confirm direct unavailability post-delete. Log/audit-only post-conditions are not API-testable.]
 * 7. Attempt to delete the same (already deleted) appeal should result in an error (e.g., not found or policy error)
 * 8. Attempt to delete a non-existent appealId (random UUID) should return an error as well
 *
 * Notes:
 * - There is no API for direct retrieval/listing of appeals or for explicit deleted_at fetch, so deletion must be validated by error on repeat/fake deletes and lack of further mutation, not by retrieval.
 * - Business expectations of audit log/compliance are out of scope for API test
 */
export async function test_api_admin_appeal_soft_delete_and_compliance(
